Potential ** SPOILERS ** for Neverwinter Nights: Hordes of the
Underdark and Nethack






The first chapter of Neverwinter Nights: Hordes of the Underdark
campaign is set in the Undermountain, a vast underground
dungeon full of nasty monsters. The place is run by Halaster
Blackcloak, a powerful and completely insane wizard, who likes to
frequently change the sections of dungeon, so that there's no way
anyone could map the thing.

In end of the first chapter, we get to meet Halaster himself. In fact,
there's *two* of him - a decoy clone and the real one. Being slightly
insane, he has a little bit of problems telling himself apart of the
clone. Or maybe the other way around. He - or maybe his clone - says
that the other one is just a double created to save him from
trouble. Yes, those words.

A randomly designed dungeon *and* a wizard who can magically clone
himself. And a specific reference to "double trouble". Hmmm.

This did create some debate regarding whichever had the idea of
"random maze with a mad mage in bottom" first, Roguelikes or the
Forgotten Realms campaign seting... =)

